WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.458 --> 00:00:02.002
[Dogs barking]

00:00:02.002 --> 00:00:04.337
I’m Mark Duplass and I play Pretzel

00:00:04.337 --> 00:00:07.048
on the new Apple TV+ original series

00:00:07.048 --> 00:00:08.341
Pretzel and the Puppies.

00:00:08.591 --> 00:00:11.553
[Dogs barking] You guys are big readers!

00:00:11.553 --> 00:00:13.638
Join us for our Pretzel Read-Along.

00:00:13.638 --> 00:00:16.433
Story time! Story time!

00:00:20.770 --> 00:00:21.354
[Dogs barking]

00:00:21.604 --> 00:00:23.773
All right, now I’m going to read Pretzel

00:00:23.773 --> 00:00:26.818
by Margret Rey with pictures by H.A. Rey.

00:00:27.444 --> 00:00:28.820
One morning in May

00:00:28.945 --> 00:00:30.947
five little dachshunds were born.

00:00:31.281 --> 00:00:33.700
One of them was Pretzel. Look how cute he is!

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:34.659
[Dogs barking]

00:00:34.659 --> 00:00:35.659
Who sees Pretzel?

00:00:35.659 --> 00:00:37.370
Which one is – that’s it! That is Pretzel.

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:38.204
That was impressive.

00:00:38.496 --> 00:00:40.832
Come on, pups. Paws up!

00:00:40.832 --> 00:00:41.708
[Dogs barking] Yeah!

00:00:41.708 --> 00:00:43.126
They grew up the way puppies do,

00:00:43.376 --> 00:00:46.880
and they all looked exactly the same for the first few weeks.

00:00:47.255 --> 00:00:49.799
But after nine weeks Pretzel

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:51.968
suddenly started growing –

00:00:52.677 --> 00:00:53.577
and growing – 

00:00:53.803 --> 00:00:54.721
and growing.

00:00:54.721 --> 00:00:58.224
He grew much longer than any of his brothers or sisters.

00:00:58.558 --> 00:00:59.809
And when he was fully grown,

00:01:00.268 --> 00:01:04.022
he had become the longest dachshund in the world!

00:01:04.314 --> 00:01:05.398
What about us? 

00:01:05.398 --> 00:01:06.398
Are we long enough?

00:01:06.649 --> 00:01:08.902
Pretzel was very pleased with himself because

00:01:08.902 --> 00:01:12.197
it is very distinguished for a dachshund to be so long.

00:01:13.114 --> 00:01:14.240
I love it!

00:01:14.616 --> 00:01:15.658
When he was one year old

00:01:15.992 --> 00:01:17.744
(a dachshund is grown up at that age)

00:01:17.744 --> 00:01:19.704
he won the Blue Ribbon at the Dog Show

00:01:19.704 --> 00:01:21.414
which means that everybody considered him

00:01:21.873 --> 00:01:23.541
the best looking dog of all.

00:01:24.042 --> 00:01:25.376
All the dogs admired him,

00:01:25.877 --> 00:01:27.337
and all the people admired him, too. 

00:01:27.712 --> 00:01:29.547
Only Greta didn’t.

00:01:30.340 --> 00:01:31.549
It’s tough when they don’t love you back.

00:01:32.342 --> 00:01:35.345
Greta was the little dachshund from across the street. 

00:01:35.595 --> 00:01:37.889
Pretzel was in love with her and he wanted to marry her. 

00:01:37.889 --> 00:01:39.265
[Greta howling]

00:01:39.265 --> 00:01:41.518
But Greta, well, she just laughed at him. 

00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:44.145
“I don’t care for long dogs,” she said.

00:01:44.395 --> 00:01:45.271
Wait, what?

00:01:45.271 --> 00:01:47.482
“But it is very distinguished for a dachshund

00:01:47.482 --> 00:01:49.317
to be so long and I

00:01:49.317 --> 00:01:51.903
won the Blue Ribbon at the Dog Show,” said Pretzel.

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:54.030
“I still don’t care,” said Greta.

00:01:54.030 --> 00:01:55.573
[Dogs barking] She still doesn’t care.

00:01:55.573 --> 00:01:56.950
[Dogs barking] What’s it going to take?

00:01:56.950 --> 00:01:58.701
[Groan]

00:01:58.701 --> 00:02:00.662
Pretzel was hurt, but he did not show it.

00:02:00.662 --> 00:02:02.163
“Please marry me,” he said. “Please!”

00:02:02.163 --> 00:02:03.206
[Dogs barking] Yes, he was begging!

00:02:03.206 --> 00:02:05.458
[Dogs barking] “Please, please marry me!

00:02:05.458 --> 00:02:06.918
And I will do anything for you,” he said.

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:09.462
“Prove it,” said Greta, and went away. 

00:02:10.004 --> 00:02:11.589
So, Pretzel set out to prove it.

00:02:11.589 --> 00:02:14.509
Now, that sure makes my tail wag!

00:02:14.884 --> 00:02:16.761
First, he bought Greta a nice bone.

00:02:16.761 --> 00:02:18.805
You guys like bones? Look at that bone.

00:02:18.888 --> 00:02:20.640
[Dogs barking] Yummy bone!

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:22.559
[Gasp] For me?

00:02:23.351 --> 00:02:24.477
“Thanks for the bone,” said Greta,

00:02:24.477 --> 00:02:28.273
“but I won’t marry you for that. I don’t care for long dogs.”

00:02:28.857 --> 00:02:29.732
Then she ate the bone

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:32.068
and then she kind of forgot about Pretzel. 

00:02:32.068 --> 00:02:34.070
Well, Pretzel had to try something else.

00:02:34.070 --> 00:02:36.156
He gave her the lovely green rubber ball

00:02:36.156 --> 00:02:37.574
he had been given for his birthday.

00:02:37.949 --> 00:02:39.200
“Thank you,” said Greta,

00:02:40.618 --> 00:02:43.705
“but I still won’t marry you because I don’t care for long dogs.

00:02:43.705 --> 00:02:45.957
Besides everybody can give presents!”

00:02:46.583 --> 00:02:49.043
And she ran away with the ball.

00:02:49.252 --> 00:02:50.003
[Dog whines] Who would do that?

00:02:50.003 --> 00:02:51.003
Who would do such a thing?

00:02:51.296 --> 00:02:54.215
“Look what I can do! Nobody except me can do that!”

00:02:54.215 --> 00:02:56.050
said Pretzel, when they met again.

00:02:56.050 --> 00:02:58.011
And this is what he did.

00:02:59.012 --> 00:03:00.763
All right, who can make a Pretzel? Let’s see it.

00:03:01.014 --> 00:03:03.099
Kind of, you do a little twisty thing? You know?

00:03:03.099 --> 00:03:05.727
Don’t get yourself all tied up in knots! 

00:03:06.144 --> 00:03:07.103
“Not bad,” said Greta.

00:03:07.896 --> 00:03:08.980
“Your name certainly fits you.

00:03:09.314 --> 00:03:11.733
But I like pretzels at the baker’s better,

00:03:12.483 --> 00:03:15.945
and I still don’t care for long dogs.”

00:03:16.279 --> 00:03:17.864
Pretzel was very unhappy.

00:03:17.864 --> 00:03:21.618
Some weeks had passed, and Greta hadn’t even spoken to Pretzel.

00:03:22.368 --> 00:03:22.952
One day,

00:03:23.328 --> 00:03:26.206
while she was playing with her green ball, it bounced away.

00:03:26.206 --> 00:03:26.915
Look!

00:03:26.915 --> 00:03:27.582
[Dog whines]

00:03:28.291 --> 00:03:30.126
Greta tried to catch it, and boomps!

00:03:30.126 --> 00:03:33.630
They both landed in a hole! Can you believe it?

00:03:33.630 --> 00:03:34.422
It’s scary!

00:03:34.756 --> 00:03:37.008
What’s going to happen? Let’s figure it out. Okay, okay.

00:03:37.008 --> 00:03:39.219
We’ll get there. I know you’re excited.

00:03:39.219 --> 00:03:42.472
You’re literally salivating to figure out what happens next.

00:03:42.472 --> 00:03:44.390
Greta tried to get out of the hole, but she couldn’t.

00:03:44.682 --> 00:03:45.683
It was much too deep.

00:03:46.309 --> 00:03:48.394
She was terribly scared.

00:03:49.062 --> 00:03:51.981
If nobody came to save her she might never, never…

00:03:52.565 --> 00:03:53.191
Just then

00:03:54.192 --> 00:03:56.694
Pretzel’s face appeared over the edge of the hole.

00:03:56.694 --> 00:03:58.363
“I’ll get you out of there!” he shouted.

00:03:58.363 --> 00:04:01.616
(He had watched Greta all the time and now he rushed to help her.)

00:04:01.950 --> 00:04:02.742
How good

00:04:03.493 --> 00:04:04.410
that Pretzel

00:04:04.911 --> 00:04:05.787
was long!

00:04:06.496 --> 00:04:08.039
“I believe you saved my life.

00:04:08.706 --> 00:04:11.251
You are wonderful!” said Greta with a sigh.

00:04:11.251 --> 00:04:13.169
“Will you marry me now?” asked Pretzel.

00:04:13.169 --> 00:04:14.087
What’s going to happen?

00:04:14.087 --> 00:04:15.505
[Dogs bark] What’s going to happen? I know, I know –

00:04:15.505 --> 00:04:17.048
it’s exciting! I know!

00:04:17.799 --> 00:04:20.385
“I will,” said Greta, “but not for your length!”

00:04:20.969 --> 00:04:23.680
So, they kissed each other, and they got married,

00:04:23.680 --> 00:04:24.931
and one morning in May

00:04:25.598 --> 00:04:28.309
five little dachshunds were born.

00:04:28.309 --> 00:04:30.061
[Dogs howl]

00:04:30.061 --> 00:04:31.479
[Dogs bark] Look at the puppies! Look!

00:04:33.106 --> 00:04:34.482
Yeah, that’s you guys!

00:04:35.275 --> 00:04:36.693
The end.

00:04:36.693 --> 00:04:37.402
[Dogs bark]

00:04:38.236 --> 00:04:40.697
Yay! Yeah! Woo!

00:04:42.031 --> 00:04:44.409
You want another story? I mean, when does it end?

00:04:44.409 --> 00:04:45.868
You’re going to have to watch the show.

00:04:46.911 --> 00:04:47.920
They can’t get enough.

